;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (ToInt and ToLong also take a char; no other conversion does), §4.3 (row byte)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of ToByte for char
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: byte
;; Only `int` and `long` take a char (cases 2853 and 2854), so `(- (int c) (int \0))` is Clojure's
;; text for a digit's value; `byte` has no instance for a char, and the checker says which
;; protocol lacks one. (`short`, `float` and `double` of a char are refused the same way.)
(defun main () -> i64 (sext i64 (byte \a)))
